What is a token?
A token is a piece of text that a language model processes.
Token --> complete word, part of word, punctuation, another text unit. (depends on a tokenizer)

What is tokenization?
Tokenization is the process of splitting text into tokens according to a tokenizer's rules.

My payment failed yesterday.

2. Tokenizer
Split the text using model-specific tokenization rules

3. Tokens
Text pieces produced by the tokenizer

4. Token IDs
Integer IDs representing the tokens in a vocabulary

5. Model input
Token IDs are converted into numerical representations for the model

Approach	How it works	Limitation or benefit
Character-level	 | Splits text into individual characters |	Long sequences for ordinary text
Word-level	| Splits text into whole words	| Very large vocabulary; unfamiliar words can be difficult to represent
Subword-level	| Splits text into reusable word pieces	| Balances vocabulary size and sequence length

