Open-source tokenizer: hands-on Python

We'll start with Hugging Face Transformers. It provides tokenizers associated with many open-weight models.
The tokenizer should match the model you're using; a different model may split the same text differently

Python text input
|
Hugging Face AutoTokenizer
Loads the tokenizer for Qwen

Install the libraries: pip install transformers


from transformers import AutoTokenizer

# Load the tokenizer associated with this model
model_name = "Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct"
tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(model_name)

# Example input
text = "My banking payment failed yesterday."

# Convert text into token IDs
token_ids = tokenizer.encode(
    text,
    add_special_tokens=False
)

# Convert token IDs back into readable token pieces
tokens = tokenizer.convert_ids_to_tokens(token_ids)

print("Original text:", text)
print("Tokens:", tokens)
print("Token IDs:", token_ids)
print("Token count:", len(token_ids))

# Reconstruct the text from the IDs
decoded_text = tokenizer.decode(token_ids)
print("Decoded text:", decoded_text)
